# portal 1.03 patch 20 — one owner per generation, and every entry through one lock
#
# PortalRuntime (Off | Starting | Active | Stopping | Failed) with a monotonic generation and
# a tunnel epoch; PortalRuntimeCoordinator serialises the power button, a row tap, Quick
# Settings, the quick action, a revoke and a restart under one mutex with the documented
# order coordinator -> transitionLock -> ServiceController.lock -> tunLock. Xray stop answers
# only after `XrayStop` returned; XrayTunHolder is locked and epoch-bound; `dup()` only from a
# live descriptor; `Active` only after the owner acknowledged the tunnel.
# Expected on the device: `PortalRuntime generation=N owner=… phase=…` lines, one Active at a
# time, no `Already closed`, no stale acknowledgement.
# Rollback: revert this patch alone; 19/19b/19c stay as they are.
